  "body": "What changed: a bore-side ring after another ring at the same level takes the entry on its\r\nfirst level and the level transition below it. Before, it took the pass link: lift, then a\r\nplunge into solid with no note. `ring_link` returns `false` when the entry must engage the\r\nlevel, and `engage_level` travels over to the lead-in first (`Step::travel`).\r\n\r\nReadings (three square bores, ramp 5 degrees, stepdown 2 mm, 6 mm deep): main posts 6 axial\r\ndives with `notes: []`. This branch posts 0, and the steepest descent is at most 5 degrees.\r\n\r\nPinning tests (`camcraft-motion`, `contour_inside_ramp`): `every_ring_of_a_multi_ring_bore_is_entered_by_the_stated_entry`\r\n(fails on main), `a_single_ring_bore_still_ramps_without_an_axial_dive`.\r\n\r\nNot exercised: the 8.5k-facet STEP plate from the report; the generation time of keep_down\r\n(issue #3831: the time is in `verify_bodies`, not in the kernel, so this PR does not change it); outside rings (the\r\nsame pass-link plunge remains there); tabbed bores (unchanged).\r\n\r\nQuick gate (`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4 cargo xtask gate quick`, Windows, `core.autocrlf=true`, 1183 steps): all other steps ok. Red: `sinumerik_810m_post`, `catalog_render`, `egui_app`, `trace_composite`, `trace_parity` (the same as main). clippy green.\r\nBaseline: the same steps on unmodified `origin/main` (run by name):\r\n- `sinumerik_810m_post`, `catalog_render` and `egui_app` are red on main too. The first two read a\r\n  golden or example file that the CRLF checkout changed. `egui_app` exits 101 on main.\r\n- `trace_composite` and `trace_parity` crash with an access violation on both main and the\r\n  branch, on some runs and not on others (main: 3 of 3 manual runs crashed, 2 gate runs passed).\r\n- `clippy -D warnings` is green on main and on this branch.\r\nNo red step is new on this branch.\r\n\r\nChangelog: A bore-side 2D Contour with several rings enters every ring by its ramp or helix, not only the first.\r\n\r\nFixes #3830\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
